{
  "Container controls for arranging other controls: `Stack` (a row or column), `Grid` (rows and columns), `Panel` (a plain box that can scroll), `GroupBox` (a titled frame), `DockPanel` (children docked to its edges) and `SplitContainer` (two panes with a splitter). All of them are controls, so they can disable and hide their content, and they lay out children added at any time.": "",
  "Children can be declared in JSX or added later with `controls.add`, and the container handles both. A child sets its own layout options through its props (`grow`, `row`, `dock`…), whatever type of component it is.": "",
  "Stack": "Stack",
  "A row or column with a gap. `align` positions children across the direction, and `justify` positions them along it. `wrap` starts a new line when they do not fit, and a child with `grow` takes the free space.": "",
  "Spacing": "Boşluklar",
  "`gap` and `padding` accept a step from the spacing scale, a number of pixels, or any CSS length.": "",
  "A step from the spacing scale: `xxs`, `xs`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl` or `xxl`, from the `layout.space.*` tokens (the design system `space.1` … `space.12`). Density and themes apply to them.": "",
  "A number is in pixels.": "",
  "Any CSS length.": "Herhangi bir CSS uzunluğu.",
  "Padding accepts one to four values, as in CSS (block-start, inline-end, block-end, inline-start), and can mix steps and lengths. The values follow the reading direction.": "",
  "Grid": "Grid",
  "Rows and columns defined in a CSS-like syntax. Children fill the cells in order, or set their position with `row`, `column`, `rowSpan` and `columnSpan`, counted from 1.": "",
  "Tracks": "İzler",
  "CSS grid tracks. A bare number is in pixels.": "",
  "`*` means `1fr`, and `2*` means `2fr`.": "",
  "Any CSS track, including functions.": "",
  "The same tracks as a list.": "",
  "A number creates that many equal columns or rows.": "",
  "Form layout": "",
  "Fixed and flexible tracks": "Sabit ve esnek izler",
  "Panel": "Panel",
  "A plain box with padding, an optional frame and its own scrolling. A scrolling panel is a Tab stop, so it can be scrolled with the keyboard, and `text` provides its name.": "",
  "GroupBox": "GroupBox",
  "A titled frame around related controls. It is a `<fieldset>`, so screen readers announce the group by its title and disabling it disables its content. The `&` key in the title moves focus to the first control, and `collapsible` lets the title show and hide the content.": "",
  "DockPanel": "DockPanel",
  "Children dock to the edges in the order they appear: `top`, `bottom`, `start` and `end` (the last two follow the reading direction), and `fill` takes the remaining space. A `float` child sits over the others at its own `left`, `top`, `right` and `bottom`. The layout uses CSS grid, so no code runs when the size changes.": "",
  "Application shell": "",
  "SplitContainer": "SplitContainer",
  "Two panes, `first` and `second`, separated by a splitter that can be dragged or moved with the keyboard. `fixedPanel` preserves the size of one pane when the container is resized, and the minimum sizes are enforced. Enter collapses the first pane and restores it. Split containers can be nested.": "",
  "Nested split containers": "İç içe split container'lar",
  "The splitter is one Tab stop between the panes, and a scrolling `Panel` is its own Tab stop.": "",
  "Moves the splitter by `step`. Left and Right follow the visual direction on right-to-left pages.": "",
  "Sets the first pane to its smallest or largest size.": "",
  "Collapses the first pane, or restores the splitter to its previous position.": "",
  "Moves focus to the first control in a `GroupBox` (Control + Option + key on Apple platforms).": "",
  "Scrolls a focused scrolling `Panel`, using the browser's default behavior.": "",
  "`role=\"separator\"`, focusable, with `aria-valuenow` (the share of the first pane, 0 to 100), `aria-valuemin`, `aria-valuemax`, `aria-orientation` and `aria-controls` for the first pane. It is named by `splitterLabel` or `uiLocale`, following the ARIA window splitter pattern.": "",
  "`inert`, so it is out of reach of Tab and screen readers. Focus inside moves to the splitter.": "",
  "A native `<fieldset>` named by its `<legend>`. When disabled, it disables the native controls inside. A collapsible group box has a button with `aria-expanded`.": "",
  "With `text`, a region landmark with that name. When scrolling, it is a Tab stop.": "",
  "Stack, Grid and DockPanel position children with CSS only. Tab and screen readers follow document order, so write children in reading order.": "",
  "The only string these containers display is the splitter name, `uiLocale.strings.resize`, unless `splitterLabel` is set.": "",
  "`data-orientation`, `data-align`, `data-justify`, `data-wrap`, `data-reverse`, `data-inline`. A growing child gets `data-mx-grow`.": "",
  "`data-align`, `data-justify`, `data-inline`. Tracks and child positions are inline grid properties.": "",
  "Each child gets `data-mx-dock`. Its position and the `gap`, a margin on the side facing the remaining area, are set inline.": "",
  "Set inline from `gap`, `rowGap` and `columnGap` (Stack, Grid, GroupBox).": "",
  "The spacing steps of `gap` and `padding`.": "`gap` ve `padding` boşluk adımları.",
  "The default gap of Stack and Grid.": "",
  "Unit: a panel (`outline` for a frame, `card` for a raised surface).": "",
  "Units: a group box (`plain`, `collapsed`), its label, the collapse button and its chevron.": "",
  "The default gap inside a group box, and the position of its label.": "",
  "Units: the splitter (`focus`), its line and its grip (`active`, `disabled`).": "Unit'ler: ayırıcı (`focus`), çizgisi ve tutacağı (`active`, `disabled`).",
  "`size` (the pointer target area), `line-width`, `active-width`, `grip-length`, `grip-thickness`.": "",
  "Every container also has the properties shared by `Control`: `enabled` and `disabled` (which apply to everything inside), `visible`, `tabStop` and `tabIndex`.": "",
  "Stack props": "Stack prop'ları",
  "`horizontal` follows the reading direction.": "`horizontal` okuma yönünü izler.",
  "The space between children.": "",
  "The space inside the edges.": "Kenarların içindeki boşluk.",
  "Alignment across the direction: `start`, `center`, `end`, `stretch` or `baseline`.": "",
  "Alignment along the direction: `start`, `center`, `end`, `space-between`, `space-around` or `space-evenly`.": "",
  "Moves children that do not fit to a new line.": "",
  "Lays out children from the opposite end. The Tab order stays in document order.": "",
  "Flows within a line of text, as wide as its children.": "",
  "Grid props": "Grid prop'ları",
  "One column": "",
  "See Tracks.": "",
  "The gap between rows and columns.": "",
  "The gap in one direction only.": "",
  "The size of implicit tracks. A number is in pixels.": "",
  "How children without a position fill the grid: `row`, `column`, `row dense` or `column dense`.": "",
  "The vertical alignment of children in their cells.": "",
  "The horizontal alignment of children in their cells.": "",
  "Flows within a line of text.": "",
  "Panel props": "Panel prop'ları",
  "Scrolls its content. It then becomes a Tab stop, so the keyboard can scroll it.": "",
  "`plain`, `outline` (a border) or `card` (a card surface).": "",
  "Names the panel, which makes it a region landmark with that name.": "",
  "GroupBox props": "GroupBox prop'ları",
  "The legend. `&Address` makes Alt+A move focus to the first control inside. This is the same property as `text`.": "",
  "Makes the title a button that shows and hides the content.": "",
  "Hides the content (with `collapsible`).": "",
  "The space inside the frame.": "Çerçevenin içindeki boşluk.",
  "The space between children, which stack in a column.": "",
  "`outline` (a frame with the title on its edge) or `plain` (the title above the content).": "",
  "DockPanel props": "DockPanel prop'ları",
  "The space between a docked child and the remaining area.": "",
  "SplitContainer props": "SplitContainer prop'ları",
  "`horizontal` places the panes side by side, as in Stack, and `vertical` stacks them.": "",
  "The size of the pane that keeps its size (the first pane with `fixedPanel=\"none\"`), in pixels, as a share, or as a CSS length. `x-model` binds it.": "",
  "The pane that keeps its size when the container is resized. With `none`, both grow and the position is kept as a share.": "",
  "The minimum size of each pane, in pixels.": "",
  "The collapsed pane. The other pane takes all the space.": "",
  "Lets the pointer and keyboard move the splitter.": "",
  "Enter and a double-click collapse and restore the first pane.": "",
  "The distance an arrow key moves the splitter, in pixels.": "",
  "The accessible name of the splitter.": "",
  "Props a child sets for its container": "",
  "Used by": "",
  "Takes the free space along the direction. Numbers share it proportionally.": "",
  "The starting line, counted from 1. A string is passed to CSS as is (`-1`).": "",
  "The number of tracks it spans.": "",
  "`top`, `bottom`, `start`, `end`, `fill` (the default) or `float`.": "",
  "The anchors of a `float` child. A number is in pixels, and `left` plus `right` stretches it.": "",
  "The two panes, as `Panel` objects: `split.first.controls.add(…)`, `split.second.scrollable = true`.": "",
  "The `role=\"separator\"` element.": "`role=\"separator\"` öğesi.",
  "Maps to `position` for `x-model`.": "",
  "The `<legend>` element.": "",
  "`void`, value": "`void`, değer",
  "Sets a child's `grow` programmatically, with a value or a function.": "",
  "Sets a child's `row`, `column`, `rowSpan` and `columnSpan` programmatically.": "",
  "Sets a child's `dock` programmatically.": "",
  "Sets the `left`, `top`, `right` and `bottom` of a `float` child.": "",
  "Collapses a pane (the first by default), or shows both panes again.": "",
  "Sets focus on the first control inside, expanding a collapsed box if needed.": "",
  "Occurs when the splitter moves (at the end of a drag), or when a pane is collapsed or restored. `e`: `{ position, collapsed, byUser, source }`.": "",
  "Occurs when the content is shown or hidden. `e`: `{ collapsed, byUser, source }`.": "",
  "`ChildSettings`, which reads a child's settings from its props and tracks children added later, is exported for use in your own containers.": ""
}
